      "text" : "Play dummy's S7 and duck the opening spade in South. On continued spades, duck again and win the third round with SA, aiming to exhaust East's spades before conceding DA. The principal source is four diamond winners after driving out DA; with SA, CA and at least three hearts these provide nine tricks. Preserve dummy's HA as the entry to established diamonds. When safely on lead in South, cash HK, HQ and HJ before leading a low diamond toward dummy's honors; continue diamonds until DA is forced out. Recover control, enter dummy with HA and cash the remaining diamonds, taking CA as needed. Successful heart unblocking gives four heart tricks and potentially ten tricks overall. If defenders switch during the hold-up, retain the same diamond-development priority and win heart leads in South where possible, keeping HA for the diamond entry. Avoid a club finesse: no extra club trick is required. The main residual danger is DA with the defender retaining enough established spades to defeat the contract; the hold-up protects against the short-spade defender holding DA, but cannot eliminate every adverse layout.",
